      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): cap pricing cache entries to prevent unbounded memory growth (#101543)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #101543. The gateway model-pricing cache (`cachedPricing` Map in `model-pricing-cache-state.ts`) has no upper bound. Long-running OpenClaw processes with many dynamic models or plugins accumulate pricing entries on every 24h refresh cycle without eviction, eventually causing OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds `MAX_PRICING_CACHE_ENTRIES = 1000` and caps the Map in `replaceGatewayModelPricingCache`. When a refresh produces more entries than the limit, excess entries are trimmed to keep memory bounded.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real behavior proof — cache cap in action\n\nBuilds 1100 entries on main (unbounded), then demonstrates the PR branch caps at 1000:\n\n```\n=== BEFORE cap (no limit) ===\nCache size: 1100 (unbounded on main)\n\n=== WITH cap (PR branch) ===\nCapped size: 1000\nEntry #1099 preserved on main, dropped with cap: true\n\n✅ Capping at 1000 prevents unbounded Map growth\n```\n\nRun with: `node --import tsx/esm -e \"import { replaceGatewayModelPricingCache, ... } from './src/gateway/model-pricing-cache-state.ts'; ...\"`\n\n### Vitest\n\n```\npnpm test src/gateway/model-pricing-cache.test.ts\n  [...] \"caps cache entries at MAX_PRICING_CACHE_ENTRIES\" — passed\n```\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/gateway/model-pricing-cache-state.ts` | +`MAX_PRICING_CACHE_ENTRIES` constant; `replaceGatewayModelPricingCache` caps incoming Map |\n| `src/gateway/model-pricing-cache.test.ts` | +1 test: cache entry cap at 1000 |\n",
        "branch": "fix/pricing-cache-bounds",
